{
  "_about": "Data for the teacher-name predicate (server/compiler/characters/naming.js; decision child-names-teacher). Lower case, Latin letters only (the charset rule admits nothing else). 'contains' entries match anywhere in the name with spaces and hyphens removed and letter runs collapsed (fuuuck), so they must be long and unambiguous; 'word' entries match a whole word or the whole name only (no Scunthorpe: 'ass' never matches Cassandra, 'love' never matches Lovely). 'phrases' match the whole name with separators removed. Extend by adding entries and a test row; never by loosening the matcher. rev 2 (2026-10-03, review of lesson-safety-naming): 'word' entries of 3+ letters also match when glued to each other or to a fixed affix (my/ur/your/mera/meri/mere/i/iam/im/the before; s/es/u/ji/ie/me/you after), so Mybaby, Babylove, Friends and Mummyji are caught while Lovely, Gopal and Nazia are not; gf/bf also match as a prefix. An AI-denial pattern on the folded name, and the floor predicate on 'I am <name>, your AI teacher', run before the lists.",
